Done. `benchmark/artifacts/lru_cache.py` — all smoke checks pass (LRU order, default arg, in-place update, lazy + explicit TTL expiry, capacity bound, thread safety under 10 concurrent workers).

```python
class LRUCache:
    def __init__(self, capacity): ...          # raises ValueError if < 1
    def get(self, key, default=None)           # hit/miss counter; expired -> miss + lazy delete
    def put(self, key, val, ttl_seconds=None)  # move-to-recent; evicts LRU on overflow (counted)
    def evict_expired()                        # returns count removed
    def stats()                                # {"hits", "misses", "evictions"}
```

Design notes: `OrderedDict` for O(1) recency, one `threading.Lock`, `_expiry[key] = time.time() + ttl`. Expired entries found via `get()` are purged and counted as misses; only capacity-driven removals count as evictions. Also added `__len__`/`__contains__` since they're trivial under the same lock — drop them if you want it strictly minimal.
